  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Engineer's Workstation",
    "overview": "The site is one developer desktop, seen at night. Every page is a tool an engineer would really have open: Home is a terminal window running a boot script, About is an IDE with a file explorer and tabs (`about-me.md`, `skills.json`), and Projects is a shell prompt where you `grep` and pass `--flags`. Navigation reads as shell commands (`cd /projects`, `cat cv.pdf`, `./login.sh`), and the footer is an editor status bar (`Online | UTF-8 | es_ES | main`). The metaphor holds because each piece behaves like the real tool, not because it's decorated like one.\n\nDensity is moderate and calm. Wide, dark fields of page-night surround bordered panes of console-black, and the content sits in those panes the way output sits in a terminal. One blue does nearly all the signalling; prompt green marks the shell's own voice. Personality lives in the copy and labels, which are command-style and witty. The shapes and states are strict and utilitarian, like well-made dev tools.\n\nThe system is dark only. It rejects the generic SaaS landing page: no gradient hero, no stock illustration, no \"trusted by\" logo strip.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Workstation metaphor: terminal, IDE, and shell, each used where it fits the content.",
      "Dark only. Layers of near-black blue-grey separated by 1px hairlines.",
      "One action color (Deploy Blue), one shell color (Prompt Green), plus a One Dark-style syntax palette for code-like content.",
      "Space Grotesk everywhere, set like a terminal font.",
      "Command-style microcopy on every control: `./view_projects.sh`, `--all`, `EXECUTE`.",
      "Window chrome (traffic lights, title bar) marks things that are \"windows\"; flat panes are everything else."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Blue Rule",
        "body": "Deploy Blue is the only color that means \"you can act here\". Green belongs to the shell, the syntax colors belong to code, and neither ever becomes a button.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Hairline Rule",
        "body": "Structure comes from 1px Hairline borders on Console Black, not from fills or shadows. If two panes need separating, give them a border.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Command Label Rule",
        "body": "Interactive labels are written as commands, scripts, or flags (`./contact_me.sh`, `--kubernetes`, `cd /about`). Shapes stay strict, so the copy carries the wit.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Window Rule",
        "body": "Only elements with window chrome (traffic lights or a title bar) get the window float shadow. A card is a pane, not a window.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do build each new surface as a tool from the workstation: a terminal transcript, an editor file, or a shell command. Pick whichever fits the content.",
      "Do write every interactive label as a command, script, path, or flag, and translate it in all four locales.",
      "Do separate panes with 1px Hairline (`#30363d`) borders on Console Black (`#0d1117`) over Page Night (`#111921`).",
      "Do reserve Deploy Blue (`#197fe6`) for action, focus, active state, and heading markers.",
      "Do use Prompt Green (`#4ade80`) only for prompts, `$` markers, and success output.",
      "Do put window chrome (traffic lights + title bar) and the Window float shadow only on true windows: the hero terminal and modals.",
      "Do color code-like data with the syntax palette, never UI controls."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't add a light mode. The workstation is dark only.",
      "Don't drift into a generic SaaS landing page: no gradient hero, no stock illustration, no \"trusted by\" logo strips.",
      "Don't add a second action color, or make green or a syntax hue clickable.",
      "Don't give flat cards the Window float shadow or fake window chrome.",
      "Don't use rounding above 12px on containers, or pill-shaped buttons.",
      "Don't add lift/scale hover motion. State changes are color and border transitions (~150ms), plus the 200ms route fade.",
      "Don't assume `font-mono` means fixed-width. It is Space Grotesk; only ASCII diagrams use a real monospace face."
    ]
  }
